{"title":"2017 AIME II Problems/Problem 12","text":"<div class=\"mw-content-ltr mw-parser-output\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><div id=\"toc\" class=\"toc\" role=\"navigation\" aria-labelledby=\"mw-toc-heading\"><input type=\"checkbox\" role=\"button\" id=\"toctogglecheckbox\" class=\"toctogglecheckbox\" style=\"display:none\" /><div class=\"toctitle\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><h2 id=\"mw-toc-heading\">Contents</h2><span class=\"toctogglespan\"><label class=\"toctogglelabel\" for=\"toctogglecheckbox\"></label></span></div>\n<ul>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-1\"><a href=\"#Problem\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">1</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Problem</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-2\"><a href=\"#Solution_1\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">2</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 1</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-3\"><a href=\"#Solution_2\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">3</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 2</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-4\"><a href=\"#Solution_3\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">4</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 3</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-5\"><a href=\"#Solution_4\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">5</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 4</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-6\"><a href=\"#Solution_5_(complex)\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">6</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 5 (complex)</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-7\"><a href=\"#Video_Solution_by_mop_2024\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">7</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Video Solution by mop 2024</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-8\"><a href=\"#See_Also\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">8</span> <span class=\"toctext\">See Also</span></a></li>\n</ul>\n</div>\n\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem\">Problem</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2017_AIME_II_Problems/Problem_12&amp;action=edit&amp;section=1\" title=\"Edit section: Problem\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Circle <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/c/e/7ce4664de7db214d4c56a42b1922cbd0fb7e7785.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$C_0$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"19\" height=\"15\" /> has radius <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/c/e/dce34f4dfb2406144304ad0d6106c5382ddd1446.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" />, and the point <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/c/c/7cce761941ab4b57ae903d05b8fa0568ebbdd98f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$A_0$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"19\" height=\"15\" /> is a point on the circle. Circle <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/0/b/70b97eb4ad6e4e7a5a97e2547d9ed6e965960d0c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$C_1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"18\" height=\"15\" /> has radius <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/9/b/b9ba1a2761691e9ca99747ef4e99c336c4639441.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$r&lt;1$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"41\" height=\"12\" /> and is internally tangent to <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/c/e/7ce4664de7db214d4c56a42b1922cbd0fb7e7785.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$C_0$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"19\" height=\"15\" /> at point <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/c/c/7cce761941ab4b57ae903d05b8fa0568ebbdd98f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$A_0$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"19\" height=\"15\" />. Point <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/6/c/36c7f3f828cf12ab9cafeffad282468a95219600.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$A_1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"23\" height=\"17\" /> lies on circle <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/0/b/70b97eb4ad6e4e7a5a97e2547d9ed6e965960d0c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$C_1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"18\" height=\"15\" /> so that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/6/c/36c7f3f828cf12ab9cafeffad282468a95219600.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$A_1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"23\" height=\"17\" /> is located <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/a/7/6a7dfa8a2a90d521b2b03f5b82a1fb9f85dce88c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$90^{\\circ}$\" width=\"24\" height=\"13\" /> counterclockwise from <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/c/c/7cce761941ab4b57ae903d05b8fa0568ebbdd98f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$A_0$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"19\" height=\"15\" /> on <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/0/b/70b97eb4ad6e4e7a5a97e2547d9ed6e965960d0c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$C_1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"18\" height=\"15\" />. Circle <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/6/5/b65e6facfe122c182fe14d503aeace2c52a9739d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$C_2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"19\" height=\"15\" /> has radius <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/2/2/e2221c84f16a3f75ae07e5023384cc40d9c05357.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$r^2$\" width=\"14\" height=\"15\" /> and is internally tangent to <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/0/b/70b97eb4ad6e4e7a5a97e2547d9ed6e965960d0c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$C_1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"18\" height=\"15\" /> at point <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/6/c/36c7f3f828cf12ab9cafeffad282468a95219600.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$A_1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"23\" height=\"17\" />. In this way a sequence of circles <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/0/c/50c00d3b0e2696191c4486f40c125033a051f5f9.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$C_1,C_2,C_3,\\ldots$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"105\" height=\"16\" /> and a sequence of points on the circles <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/5/7/a576196a316dd523a75953de56669e2226d1ec13.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$A_1,A_2,A_3,\\ldots$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"111\" height=\"18\" /> are constructed, where circle <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/e/1/4e173907ca992482385a50c6f62ede920362b1bf.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$C_n$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"21\" height=\"15\" /> has radius <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/4/9/d4988535e75f49421ac5f095608f3048782b7e78.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$r^n$\" width=\"16\" height=\"12\" /> and is internally tangent to circle <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/e/e/7eeb85f27b76e421673cf261935886286041d551.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$C_{n-1}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"37\" height=\"15\" /> at point <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/c/b/bcb9b7352942e18a3df49fadca0f6a49f3508209.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$A_{n-1}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"37\" height=\"15\" />, and point <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/e/c/1eccfbd65334353f671fb71c27b9b9f2c689b0bf.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$A_n$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"21\" height=\"15\" /> lies on <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/e/1/4e173907ca992482385a50c6f62ede920362b1bf.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$C_n$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"21\" height=\"15\" /> <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/a/7/6a7dfa8a2a90d521b2b03f5b82a1fb9f85dce88c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$90^{\\circ}$\" width=\"24\" height=\"13\" /> counterclockwise from point <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/c/b/bcb9b7352942e18a3df49fadca0f6a49f3508209.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$A_{n-1}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"37\" height=\"15\" />, as shown in the figure below. There is one point <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/f/5/ff5fb3d775862e2123b007eb4373ff6cc1a34d4e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$B$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"17\" height=\"14\" /> inside all of these circles. When <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/1/3/b13b5cee4d456ee4c266f1a793082af548430e98.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$r = \\frac{11}{60}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -12px\" width=\"53\" height=\"37\" />, the distance from the center <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/c/e/7ce4664de7db214d4c56a42b1922cbd0fb7e7785.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$C_0$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"19\" height=\"15\" /> to <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/f/5/ff5fb3d775862e2123b007eb4373ff6cc1a34d4e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$B$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"17\" height=\"14\" /> is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/7/f/27f583697295fc6f723862c13228ee55107c33ca.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{m}{n}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"22\" height=\"34\" />, where <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/5/0/f5047d1e0cbb50ec208923a22cd517c55100fa7b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$m$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"18\" height=\"10\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/7/4/174fadd07fd54c9afe288e96558c92e0c1da733a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"13\" height=\"10\" /> are relatively prime positive integers. Find <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/2/d/02dbab3601fa6cce490d54263017048f69e1a35d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$m+n$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"51\" height=\"14\" />.\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/7/1/e7152ffa3581f7f843ccb938b74c8468a3d156c5.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"[asy] draw(Circle((0,0),125)); draw(Circle((25,0),100)); draw(Circle((25,20),80)); draw(Circle((9,20),64)); dot((125,0)); label(&quot;$A_0$&quot;,(125,0),E); dot((25,100)); label(&quot;$A_1$&quot;,(25,100),SE); dot((-55,20)); label(&quot;$A_2$&quot;,(-55,20),E); [/asy]\" width=\"252\" height=\"222\" />\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_1\">Solution 1</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2017_AIME_II_Problems/Problem_12&amp;action=edit&amp;section=2\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 1\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Impose a coordinate system and let the center of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/c/e/7ce4664de7db214d4c56a42b1922cbd0fb7e7785.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$C_0$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"19\" height=\"15\" /> be <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/9/6/f9603ca3089464e548fc6f1366bc474e7efef8d9.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(0,0)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"42\" height=\"20\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/c/c/7cce761941ab4b57ae903d05b8fa0568ebbdd98f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$A_0$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"19\" height=\"15\" /> be <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/5/a/25a306093bbd9e0699c65dba033c9483cd379dc4.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(1,0)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"42\" height=\"20\" />. Therefore <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/8/6/e86b7d4f500616d7fc591ee24bb846380320dee7.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$A_1=(1-r,r)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"113\" height=\"18\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/a/1/5a103d3307332133f5422caacd08af7293c3447a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$A_2=(1-r-r^2,r-r^2)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"191\" height=\"19\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/8/b/f8b5dc83ae8990d2c27ef98dafca87b0e914b489.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$A_3=(1-r-r^2+r^3,r-r^2-r^3)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"268\" height=\"19\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/f/b/bfb023f19eaf62792077d47dda913540eccb2b14.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$A_4=(1-r-r^2+r^3+r^4,r-r^2-r^3+r^4)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"345\" height=\"19\" />, and so on, where the signs alternate in groups of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/1/c/41c544263a265ff15498ee45f7392c5f86c6d151.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" />. The limit of all these points is point <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/f/5/ff5fb3d775862e2123b007eb4373ff6cc1a34d4e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$B$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"17\" height=\"14\" />. Using the sum of infinite geometric series formula on <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/f/5/ff5fb3d775862e2123b007eb4373ff6cc1a34d4e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$B$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"17\" height=\"14\" /> and reducing the expression: <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/5/0/a5083360d19e7aedb8bb8727d06b7a790baa12a3.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(1-r)-(r^2-r^3)+(r^4-r^5)-...=\\frac{1-r}{1+r^2}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -15px\" width=\"351\" height=\"40\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/6/8/f6852fa76a182fa7ea649545aee5838630f4515f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(r-r^2)-(r^3-r^4)+(r^5-r^6)-...=\\frac{r-r^2}{1+r^2}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -15px\" width=\"358\" height=\"42\" />. Thus, we get <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/6/6/566f759c68cfa1610ffd6533620bf4b46302c54f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$B=\\left(\\frac{1-r}{r^2+1},\\frac{r-r^2}{r^2+1}\\right)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -17px\" width=\"172\" height=\"43\" />. The distance from <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/f/5/ff5fb3d775862e2123b007eb4373ff6cc1a34d4e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$B$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"17\" height=\"14\" /> to the origin is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/b/e/bbef0e2481f805e42af0ce9df3558d6375c38e06.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\sqrt{\\left(\\frac{1-r}{r^2+1}\\right)^2+\\left(\\frac{r-r^2}{r^2+1}\\right)^2}=\\frac{1-r}{\\sqrt{r^2+1}}.$\" style=\"vertical-align: -18px\" width=\"304\" height=\"53\" /> Let <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/4/1/a41bd5a6a96ecc43c81e5455afa2fdc9acbf1b5d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$r=\\frac{11}{60}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"57\" height=\"38\" />, and the distance from the origin is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/3/b/13b6dd393c8553da70329e0572be7e8e4b6c1ad4.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{49}{61}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"20\" height=\"38\" />.  <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/4/a/e4a83da0abbe3e054748417a3cbcacceffb0133a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$49+61=\\boxed{110}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"122\" height=\"23\" />.\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_2\">Solution 2</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2017_AIME_II_Problems/Problem_12&amp;action=edit&amp;section=3\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 2\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Let the center of circle <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/1/1/c117e8403b3b9cf74d2f63f6627aa17c1995e3bc.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$C_i$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"17\" height=\"15\" /> be <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/9/d/29d2497c8595ac7c5d96326b5c0174cc44d77c8c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$O_i$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"18\" height=\"15\" />. Note that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/0/6/f064959bd73ec5749990acf852dd9733a8ae5c53.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$O_0BO_1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"55\" height=\"15\" /> is a right triangle, with right angle at <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/f/5/ff5fb3d775862e2123b007eb4373ff6cc1a34d4e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$B$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"17\" height=\"14\" />. Also, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/e/0/ee04a1bd75ff5d2770e387a8f5c22b7df3a9e3cc.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$O_1B=\\frac{11}{60}O_0B$\" style=\"vertical-align: -12px\" width=\"117\" height=\"37\" />, or <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/3/6/b36b665e439a49353da11a285d399d3c42cac3d7.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$O_0B = \\frac{60}{61}O_0O_1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"123\" height=\"38\" />. It is clear that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/1/6/c161b14956c5865b52b663bd2e88f54bcb8c39a3.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$O_0O_1=1-r=\\frac{49}{60}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -12px\" width=\"151\" height=\"37\" />, so <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/0/6/806b62f1e6e3d96c2055f4ca234a70152d1f0f22.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$O_0B=\\frac{60}{61}\\times\\frac{49}{60}=\\frac{49}{61}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"171\" height=\"38\" />. Our answer is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/4/a/e4a83da0abbe3e054748417a3cbcacceffb0133a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$49+61=\\boxed{110}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"122\" height=\"23\" />\n</p><p>-william122\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_3\">Solution 3</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2017_AIME_II_Problems/Problem_12&amp;action=edit&amp;section=4\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 3\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Note that there is an invariance, Consider the entire figure <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/d/f/7df6156885f7ecb884a812ae7155a0ad3ea33684.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\mathcal{F}$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"15\" height=\"13\" />. Perform a <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/2/e/22ec0d2e4202839322d26a23dcb13f79821df5d7.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$90^\\circ$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"28\" height=\"15\" /> counterclockwise rotation, then scale by <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/5/5/b55ca7a0aa88ab7d58f4fc035317fdac39b17861.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$r$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"10\" /> with respect to <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/5/4/754e946d1a160f767f0f61cbd9460401c2d1c17f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(1, 0)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"38\" height=\"18\" />. It is easy to see that the new figure <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/d/d/4ddab635a11a5881fd3628c3c17d34f176946c6c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\mathcal{F}&#39; \\cup S^1 = \\mathcal{F}$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"99\" height=\"15\" />, so <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/f/5/ff5fb3d775862e2123b007eb4373ff6cc1a34d4e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$B$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"17\" height=\"14\" /> is invariant.\n</p><p>Using the invariance, Let <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/c/2/4c2722581081aff52ab1403e68ad846d6c472178.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$B = (x,y)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"79\" height=\"18\" />. Then rotating and scaling, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/9/7/f972fc8ee680ddecc1b6b41f952d36167b5b8215.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$B = (1-r(1+y), rx)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"174\" height=\"18\" />. Equating, we find <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/7/0/1709ae1bc0810381de03f17fbaf06996cf6398aa.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x = \\frac{1-r}{r^2+1}, y = \\frac{r-r^2}{r^2+1}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -14px\" width=\"177\" height=\"40\" />. The distance is thus <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/3/b/13b6dd393c8553da70329e0572be7e8e4b6c1ad4.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{49}{61}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"20\" height=\"38\" />. Our answer is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/4/a/e4a83da0abbe3e054748417a3cbcacceffb0133a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$49+61=\\boxed{110}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"122\" height=\"23\" />\n</p><p>-Isogonal\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_4\">Solution 4</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2017_AIME_II_Problems/Problem_12&amp;action=edit&amp;section=5\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 4\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Using the invariance again as in Solution 3, assume <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/f/5/ff5fb3d775862e2123b007eb4373ff6cc1a34d4e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$B$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"17\" height=\"14\" /> is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/6/a/96ab646de7704969b91c76a214126b45f2b07b25.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$d$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> away from the origin. The locus of possible points is a circle with radius <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/6/a/96ab646de7704969b91c76a214126b45f2b07b25.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$d$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" />. Consider the following diagram.\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/0/d/60d42e0ed9405ca7b2eb5e5c0d52fbf20f5eea07.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"[asy] size(7cm); draw(circle((0,0), 49/61)); draw((0,0)--(0.790110185, 0.144853534)); draw((0,0)--(-0.144853534, 0.790110185)); draw((-0.144853534, 0.790110185)--(1,0)); draw((0,0)--(1,0)); draw(rightanglemark((-0.144853534, 0.790110185), (0,0), (0.790110185, 0.144853534), 3));  label(&quot;$O$&quot;, (0,0), SW); label(&quot;$(1,0)$&quot;, (1,0), E); label(&quot;$B$&quot;, (0.790110185, 0.144853534), NE); label(&quot;$B&#39;$&quot;, (-0.144853534, 0.790110185), N); label(&quot;$d$&quot;, (0.5 * 49/61, 0), S);  [/asy]\" width=\"332\" height=\"272\" />\n</p><p>Let the distance from <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/f/5/ff5fb3d775862e2123b007eb4373ff6cc1a34d4e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$B$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"17\" height=\"14\" /> to <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/5/a/25a306093bbd9e0699c65dba033c9483cd379dc4.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(1,0)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"42\" height=\"20\" /> be <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/6/e/26eeb5258ca5099acf8fe96b2a1049c48c89a5e6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"12\" height=\"10\" />. As <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/f/5/ff5fb3d775862e2123b007eb4373ff6cc1a34d4e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$B$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"17\" height=\"14\" /> is invariant, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/8/b/d8b10666ddf4b57da3579a0267576b4271f26c17.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x = r(BB&#39; + x) \\implies x = r\\frac{d\\sqrt{2}}{1-r}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"259\" height=\"41\" />. Then by Power of a Point, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/4/8/948834ef89b6c722f1699876f9bbbec79800b551.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x(BB&#39; + x) = (1-d)(1+d) \\implies xr(BB&#39; + x) = r(1-d)(1+d) \\implies x^2 = r(1-d^2) \\implies d^2 = \\left(1 + \\frac{2r}{(1-r)^2}\\right)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -17px\" width=\"890\" height=\"43\" />. Solving, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/a/9/1a9ffc61c897f48be9a8beac9bf7507846d3dd6d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$d = \\frac{49}{61}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"54\" height=\"38\" />. Our answer is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/4/a/e4a83da0abbe3e054748417a3cbcacceffb0133a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$49+61=\\boxed{110}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"122\" height=\"23\" />\n</p><p>-Isogonal\n</p>\n<h2><span id=\"Solution_5_.28complex.29\"></span><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_5_(complex)\">Solution 5 (complex)</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2017_AIME_II_Problems/Problem_12&amp;action=edit&amp;section=6\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 5 (complex)\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Let <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/c/c/7cce761941ab4b57ae903d05b8fa0568ebbdd98f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$A_0$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"19\" height=\"15\" /> be the origin. Now note that the ratio of lengths of consecutive line segments is constant and equal to <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/5/5/b55ca7a0aa88ab7d58f4fc035317fdac39b17861.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$r$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"10\" />. Now accounting for rotation by <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/e/e/aeebb746f8c0d3dac5219c3635617032430afee9.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{\\pi}{2}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"17\" height=\"34\" /> radians, we see that the common ratio is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/f/5/cf5b788b975e0b1cbe7bcaf531fdc9997b6ba165.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$ri$\" width=\"14\" height=\"12\" />. Thus since our first term is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/1/6/d166e3fc737bed0278ba92478ad86a4697469e57.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$A_1=-r+ri$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"107\" height=\"17\" />, the total sum (by geometric series formula) is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/0/f/10f837fa0cbddea9fa6c9230b58ae638b275349c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{-r+ri}{1-ri}=\\frac{-781+538i}{3721}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -15px\" width=\"191\" height=\"40\" />. We need the distance from <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/a/6/ca6ae52dde41ee1f005d82b8879288984307566b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$C_0=-1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"70\" height=\"17\" /> so our distance is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/a/1/da1c29cdb503e4ec232fdfc100e70fd7a79b5ff9.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$|B-C_0|=\\sqrt{\\left(\\frac{-781}{3721}-(-1)\\right)^2+\\left(\\frac{538i}{3721}\\right)^2}=\\sqrt{\\frac{2401}{3721}}=\\frac{49}{61}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -20px\" width=\"475\" height=\"56\" />. Our answer is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/4/a/e4a83da0abbe3e054748417a3cbcacceffb0133a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$49+61=\\boxed{110}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"122\" height=\"23\" />\n</p><p>-chrisdiamond10\n</p><p>By the way, <a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"https://www.geogebra.org/calculator/wrtgmqmq\">here's</a> a Geogebra Diagram. ~r00tsOfUnity\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Video_Solution_by_mop_2024\">Video Solution by mop 2024</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2017_AIME_II_Problems/Problem_12&amp;action=edit&amp;section=7\" title=\"Edit section: Video Solution by mop 2024\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p><a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external free\" href=\"https://youtube.com/watch?v=5keaS1CZlLo\">https://youtube.com/watch?v=5keaS1CZlLo</a>\n</p><p>~r00tsOfUnity\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"See_Also\">See Also</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2017_AIME_II_Problems/Problem_12&amp;action=edit&amp;section=8\" title=\"Edit section: See Also\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<table class=\"wikitable\" style=\"margin:0.5em auto; font-size:95%; border:1px solid black; width:80%;\">\n<tbody><tr>\n<td style=\"background:#ccf;text-align:center;\" colspan=\"3\"><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2017_AIME_II\" title=\"2017 AIME II\">2017 AIME II</a></b> (<b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2017_AIME_II_Problems\" title=\"2017 AIME II Problems\">Problems</a></b> • <b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2017_AIME_II_Answer_Key\" title=\"2017 AIME II Answer Key\">Answer Key</a></b> • <a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"http://www.artofproblemsolving.com/Forum/resources.php?c=182&amp;cid=45&amp;year=2017\">Resources</a>)\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td width=\"50%\" align=\"center\" rowspan=\"1\">Preceded&#160;by<br /><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2017_AIME_II_Problems/Problem_11\" title=\"2017 AIME II Problems/Problem 11\">Problem 11</a></b>\n</td>\n<td width=\"50%\" align=\"center\" rowspan=\"1\">Followed&#160;by<br /><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2017_AIME_II_Problems/Problem_13\" title=\"2017 AIME II Problems/Problem 13\">Problem 13</a></b>\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td colspan=\"3\" style=\"text-align:center;\"><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2017_AIME_II_Problems/Problem_1\" title=\"2017 AIME II Problems/Problem 1\">1</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2017_AIME_II_Problems/Problem_2\" title=\"2017 AIME II Problems/Problem 2\">2</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2017_AIME_II_Problems/Problem_3\" title=\"2017 AIME II Problems/Problem 3\">3</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2017_AIME_II_Problems/Problem_4\" title=\"2017 AIME II Problems/Problem 4\">4</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2017_AIME_II_Problems/Problem_5\" title=\"2017 AIME II Problems/Problem 5\">5</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2017_AIME_II_Problems/Problem_6\" title=\"2017 AIME II Problems/Problem 6\">6</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2017_AIME_II_Problems/Problem_7\" title=\"2017 AIME II Problems/Problem 7\">7</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2017_AIME_II_Problems/Problem_8\" title=\"2017 AIME II Problems/Problem 8\">8</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2017_AIME_II_Problems/Problem_9\" title=\"2017 AIME II Problems/Problem 9\">9</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2017_AIME_II_Problems/Problem_10\" title=\"2017 AIME II Problems/Problem 10\">10</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2017_AIME_II_Problems/Problem_11\" title=\"2017 AIME II Problems/Problem 11\">11</a> <b>•</b> <a class=\"mw-selflink selflink\">12</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2017_AIME_II_Problems/Problem_13\" title=\"2017 AIME II Problems/Problem 13\">13</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2017_AIME_II_Problems/Problem_14\" title=\"2017 AIME II Problems/Problem 14\">14</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2017_AIME_II_Problems/Problem_15\" title=\"2017 AIME II Problems/Problem 15\">15</a>\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td align=\"center\" colspan=\"3\"><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=AIME_Problems_and_Solutions\" title=\"AIME Problems and Solutions\"> All AIME Problems and Solutions</a></b>\n</td></tr></tbody></table>\n<div class=\"print\">\n<div style=\"display:flex;width:100%;justify-content:space-between;align-items:center\">\n<div>\n<p><span class=\"mw-default-size\" typeof=\"mw:File\"><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=File:AMC_Logo.png\" class=\"mw-file-description\"><img src=\"https://artofproblemsolving.com/wiki/images/d/d1/AMC_Logo.png\" decoding=\"async\" width=\"97\" height=\"84\" class=\"mw-file-element\" /></a></span>\n</p>\n</div>\n<div style=\"flex-grow:1;text-align:right\">\n<p>These problems are copyrighted &#169; by the <a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"https://www.maa.org\">Mathematical Association of America</a>. \n</p>\n</div>\n<div style=\"clear:both;\"></div>\n</div></div>\n<!-- \nNewPP limit report\nCached time: 20261018002501\nCache expiry: 86400\nReduced expiry: false\nComplications: [show‐toc]\nCPU time usage: 0.049 seconds\nReal time usage: 0.072 seconds\nPreprocessor visited node count: 570/1000000\nPost‐expand include size: 1810/2097152 bytes\nTemplate argument size: 132/2097152 bytes\nHighest expansion depth: 3/100\nExpensive parser function count: 0/100\nUnstrip recursion depth: 0/20\nUnstrip post‐expand size: 18337/5000000 bytes\n-->\n<!--\nTransclusion expansion time report (%,ms,calls,template)\n100.00%   12.725      1 -total\n 57.86%    7.363      1 Template:AIME_box\n 39.72%    5.055      1 Template:MAA_Notice\n-->\n\n<!-- Saved in parser cache with key wiki-wiki_:pcache:15523:|#|:idhash:canonical and timestamp 20261018002501 and revision id 212351. Rendering was triggered because: api-parse\n -->\n</div>"}